            <ArticleTitle>Flare up of Nickel Contact Dermatits Following Oral Challenge.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient having contact dermatitis due to nickel on the wrist, sides of neck, thighs and legs, confirmed by patch tests with nickel sulphate, showed aggravation of the dermatitis following oral provocation with 25 mg nickel sulphate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
